From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:53:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add embedder-timed script animations to the servo animation
 sets

Web Animations (Element.animate) need the same cascade as CSS
animations: keyframes computed against the element's style, implicit
end keyframes, per-keyframe easing, and interpolation into the
Animations level. The servo build only knows CSS animations, which it
times itself from the animation-* properties. A ScriptAnimation carries
keyframes and a progress the embedder sets. stylo builds its computed
keyframes during the traversal (rebuilding when the element's
non-animation rules change) and samples it after the element's CSS
animations, which is their composite order.

The keyframe easing epsilon matches Blink's kBezierEpsilon: solving
more tightly shifts the sixth digit pages read back from
getComputedStyle.
